{
  "headline": "Four Syrian security personnel killed in Hama countryside attack",
  "pages": [
    {
      "text": "Four members of the Syrian Arab Republic’s Road Security forces were killed by unidentified gunmen on the Salamiyah-Athriya road in the Hama countryside, according to the Syrian Interior Ministry. Ministry spokesman Noureddine Al-Baba stated, via the state news agency Sana, that the attackers targeted two patrols on the road. While the Interior Ministry reported four fatalities, the North Press Agency reported that three road security personnel were killed on Tuesday in an attack by unidentified gunmen in the Hama countryside of central Syria. A security source told Syria’s Al-Ikhbariya TV that security forces were mobilized to investigate the incident and pursue those involved."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "headline": "Advance voter turnout increases for 2026 municipal election in Toronto, Canada",
  "pages": [
    {
      "text": "Advance voting for Toronto’s 2026 municipal election saw 222,550 eligible voters participate during a six-day period that ended at 7 p.m. on October 11, 2026. According to CBC Toronto, this represents the largest advance voter turnout in over a decade and a nearly 72 per cent increase compared to the 129,000 early votes recorded during the 2023 mayoral byelection. Election day is scheduled for October 26, 2026. On that day, eligible voters must cast ballots at their assigned voting places as indicated on their Voter Information Card or the Toronto Elections webpage. Voters who requested to vote by mail were required to return completed packages to Toronto Elections by noon on October 14, 2026. To meet this deadline, the city advised using one of 25 secure, indoor, yellow Toronto Elections Mail-in Voting drop boxes located in each ward. These boxes are monitored by CCTV and emptied daily by staff. Additionally, registration for third party advertisers, which includes any person, corporation, or trade union intending to spend money to promote, support, or oppose a candidate, closed at 4:30 p.m. on October 9, 2026. Registrations were required to be filed in person at the Toronto Elections City Hall office."
    }
  ]
}

